;; Exact example transcribed from docs/reference/language/continuations.md's
;; "Re-invocable (multi-shot) continuations" section (the doc's own claimed
;; demonstration of full multi-shot re-entrant call/cc).
;;
;; MEASURED BEHAVIOR (2026-08-25, .icc/silent-wrong-ledger.yaml SW-52):
;;   native JIT (-r): correct — prints "1" "2" "3" "done", exit 0.
;;   native AOT:      correct — prints "1" "2" "3" "done", exit 0.
;;   bytecode VM:     WRONG — prints "1" then an unbounded stream of "2",
;;                    forever. Does not terminate: the VM's own runaway-
;;                    instruction safety net (ESHKOL_VM_MAX_INSN, default
;;                    10,000,000) does not fire either, because the local
;;                    instruction counter in the dispatch loop is
;;                    reinitialised every time a continuation invocation
;;                    unwinds back into that loop, so the counter never
;;                    accumulates far enough to trip.
;;
;; Why native "works" here: this specific shape re-enters entirely within
;; the same top-level flow (no intervening function call has returned), so
;; the setjmp/longjmp jmp_buf target is still live stack. It is NOT evidence
;; of general multi-shot support — see reentry_after_function_return.esk and
;; generator_coroutine.esk in this directory for shapes where a captured
;; continuation's frame has actually returned before re-invocation, which is
;; the case escape-only (setjmp/longjmp) implementations cannot handle.
;;
;; This fixture is deliberately NOT wired into any pass/fail CI harness: the
;; VM run does not terminate. Run manually with a timeout, e.g.:
;;   ESHKOL_VM_NO_DISASM=1 ./build/eshkol-vm-standalone-test \
;;     tests/continuations/doc_example_multishot.esk   # (kill after a few seconds)
(define k #f)
(define n 0)
(display (+ 1 (call/cc (lambda (c) (set! k c) 0))))
(newline)
(set! n (+ n 1))
(if (< n 3) (k n))
(display "done") (newline)
